We turn to \eqref{eq-secondt}. For every $x\in X$, we have
\begin{equation}
    \left|\int L(x,y) \, \mathrm{d}\mu(y)\right||\tilde{\varphi}(x)|
    =\left|\int L(x,y) {\varphi}(y)\, \mathrm{d}\mu(y)\right|
\end{equation}
 \begin{equation}
    \le \left|\int L(x,y) \, \mathrm{d}\mu(y)\right| \sup_{x'\in X}
