be given as in \Cref{Holder-van-der-Corput}.
Set
\begin{equation} t:=(1+d_B({\vartheta},{\theta}))^{-\frac{\tau}{2+a}}
\end{equation}
and define $\tilde{\varphi}$ as in \Cref{Lipschitz-Holder-approximation}. Let ${\vartheta}$ and ${\theta}$ be in ${\Theta}$.

Then
   \begin{equation} \left|\int e({\vartheta}(x)-{{\theta}(x)}) \varphi (x)\, \mathrm{d}\mu(x)\right|
   \end{equation}
    \begin{equation} \le \left|\int e({\vartheta}(x)-{{\theta}(x)}) \tilde{\varphi} (x)\, \mathrm{d}\mu(x)\right|
   \end{equation}
         \begin{equation} + \left|\int e({\vartheta}(x)-{{\theta}(x)}) (\varphi (x)-\tilde{\varphi}(x))\, \mathrm{d}\mu(x)\right|
   \end{equation}

